From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: support full DSC ICH error precision

Xiaomi's Uke display source enables full ICH error precision on DSC 1.2
blocks from MDSS major version 10 onward. Its encoder sets ENC_DF_CTRL
bit 12 only when that feature is present and bits per component exceeds 8.
Add the corresponding capability and guard; the isolated SM7675 catalog
admits it separately. Other catalogs retain their existing programming.

Source: Xiaomi display-drivers, commit
44275c404a677d9d9e5230fedd1af2ef02fc7b9a,
msm/sde/sde_hw_catalog.c and msm/sde/sde_hw_dsc_1_2.c.
Both files are GPL-2.0-only, copyright The Linux Foundation and Qualcomm
Innovation Center, Inc. This candidate does not change initial_lines or
qualify panel output.

Signed-off-by: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_catalog.h | 2 ++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_dsc_1_2.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_catalog.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_catalog.h
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_catalog.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_catalog.h
@@ -143,10 +143,12 @@ enum {
 /**
  * DSC sub-blocks/features
  * @DPU_DSC_NATIVE_42x_EN     Supports NATIVE_422_EN and NATIVE_420_EN encoding
+ * @DPU_DSC_FULL_ICH_PREC     Supports full ICH error precision above 8 bpc
  * @DPU_DSC_MAX
  */
 enum {
 	DPU_DSC_NATIVE_42x_EN = 0x1,
+	DPU_DSC_FULL_ICH_PREC,
 	DPU_DSC_MAX
 };
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_dsc_1_2.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_dsc_1_2.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_dsc_1_2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_dsc_1_2.c
@@ -124,6 +124,10 @@ static void dpu_hw_dsc_config_1_2(struct dpu_hw_dsc *hw_dsc,
 
 	data |= (_dsc_calc_output_buf_max_addr(hw_dsc, num_active_slice_per_enc) << 18);
 
+	if ((hw_dsc->caps->features & BIT(DPU_DSC_FULL_ICH_PREC)) &&
+	    dsc->bits_per_component > 8)
+		data |= BIT(12);
+
 	DPU_REG_WRITE(hw, sblk->enc.base + ENC_DF_CTRL, data);
 
 	data = (dsc->dsc_version_minor & 0xf) << 28;
--
2.53.0
